# .gitignore — chapter 七百六 / M2187 第一刀
#
# Created when the Rust pilot's Cargo target/ tree
# accidentally landed in a commit and had to be reset。
# Same patterns also cover Swift Package Manager .build/
# and the legacy Xcode build/ directory the substrate
# had been tracking via implicit `git add` discipline
# rather than a .gitignore — formalize the contract here。

# ============================================================
# Swift Package Manager
# ============================================================
.build/
.swiftpm/xcode/
DerivedData/

# ============================================================
# Cargo (chapter 七百六 Rust pilot)
# ============================================================
Cargo/target/
**/target/CACHEDIR.TAG
**/*.rs.bk

# ============================================================
# Xcode user state
# ============================================================
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdatad/
xcuserdata/

# ============================================================
# macOS Finder
# ============================================================
.DS_Store

# ============================================================
# Editor
# ============================================================
*.swp
*~

# ============================================================
# Sovereign secrets + device cert-log pulls (audit 2026-06-12)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Device "Documents" pulls (Docs/cert-logs/dual-device-*) carry the
# device's bas-sovereign-host.key (32-byte Ed25519/HMAC signing keys)
# + the sqlite ledger DBs. NEVER commit those — a committed signing key
# is a CRITICAL secret exposure. Guard the key + DB classes globally and
# the bulky raw-pull archives wholesale; commit only hand-extracted log
# EXCERPTS under Docs/cert-logs/ when evidence must be in-repo.
# ============================================================
*.key
bas-sovereign-host.key
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
Docs/cert-logs/dual-device-*/
